Z||000000||Philphine||10-23-2001||10:58 AM||||<BR>just something i'm wondering with so many including myself fighting with shift action. i'm having my problems with my isuzu 5 speed. my 4 speed shifts great. i've had the 5 much longer so it could be something i do that just hasn't affected the 4 yet. i've also heard the deal about the isuzu 5's having a weak fork.<P>so which do you have? or if you have experience with a few which has given the most trouble. part of my asking is because i have an extra 4 speed (with shifter and cables) and if i get to the point of changing engines, i may change the tranny too. thanks for any input.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||10-23-2001||11:06 AM||||I've never had a clutch problem with my Izusu. That fork thing about the izusu is also just a myth. Archie uses it with his v8's all the time. I think it shifts a lot better than my Getrag.<P>Check this out <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014510.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014510.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000002||stsmithgt||10-23-2001||04:07 PM||||I have a 4spd in my 86GT.  The fork forked up in mine and slipped out of place damaging the clutch parts that were recently installed.  I guess they didn't notice that the fork was giving up the ghost.  Oh well, it's only money.............................<BR>. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .......................THAT TOOK ME FOREVER TO SAVE UP!!!!!!!!   I hope you have better luck than I have with repairs.||||reg||9
Z||000003||FieroPerformance||10-23-2001||04:47 PM||||What are some good indications that the fork needs to be replaced? I have it all out of my car right now for my engine rebuild, I am putting in a heavy duty clutch also. (BTW, I have an Isuzu 5 speed). It is very hard to shift compared to some other cars, but I think the problem is that the cables aren't routed correctly around the air intake tube.<P>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
